# LongCat 2.5 — findings by Big Pickle

- Source: OpenCode (`opencode/big-pickle`)
- Date: 2026-10-22 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **SELF-EXCLUSION — zero verified public benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID.**
> Meituan has never released a GA "LongCat 2.5". The only 2.5-line model that exists is
> `LongCat-2.5-Preview` (released 2026-09-25), which is documented separately in
> `../longcat-2.5-preview/Big_Pickle.md`. There is no GA checkpoint, no GA API id, no GA
> weights and no GA benchmark, so every row below reads "no verified public score found" for
> the ID this folder stands for. Scores are intentionally withheld rather than fabricated —
> saved as `.md.excluded` per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`.

## Model card

- **Name:** LongCat 2.5 (GA — does not exist as of 2026-10-22)
- **Short description:** Not a released model. The LongCat family by Meituan currently ends at
  **LongCat-2.5-Preview**, an API-only preview of the 1.6T-parameter sparse-MoE agentic-coding
  line. The vendor's own change log has no GA 2.5 entry, and its pay-as-you-go pricing page states
  that "Pay-As-You-Go currently supports LongCat-2.5-Preview" — so no GA endpoint can be called.
  The best-documented description of the intended GA release comes from the same vendor's
  September 2026 ecosystem report: "Buyers needing verified coding benchmarks, SLAs, or enterprise
  access controls should wait for the 2.5 GA" — i.e. the GA was still pending.
- **Provider / access:** None. The configured id `opencode/longcat-2.5` does not resolve: the
  official OpenCode Zen catalogue lists only `longcat-2.5-preview-free` (free, limited time,
  zero-retention) for this family, with no `longcat-2.5` entry, paid or free.
- **Release / knowledge:** N/A (no GA release). The preview's release date is 2026-09-25 and no
  knowledge-cutoff date is published for any LongCat checkpoint.
- **IDs:** `opencode/longcat-2.5` (configured for this folder — **does not resolve**). The only
  live 2.5-line ids are `opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free` (OpenCode Zen),
  `meituan/longcat-2.5-preview` (Vercel AI Gateway / OpenCode Data) and `LongCat-2.5-Preview`
  (LongCat API Platform).
- **Context window:** N/A for a GA model. The preview advertises 1,048,576 tokens in / 131,072 out
  (Vercel, OpenCode Data, LongCat quick-start docs), with some hosts listing 262,144 max output.
- **Modalities:** N/A for a GA model. The preview is text + image in, text out, reasoning and tool
  calling supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-22):** No GA price list exists. The preview's limited-time rates are
  $0.30 input / $0.006 cached input / $1.20 output per 1M, and every one of them is flagged
  "limited-time" with no end date and **no published undiscounted list price** — an unusual pricing
  state that alone argues against quoting a GA price.
- **Architecture:** N/A for a GA model. The preview is proprietary / API-only (no 2.5 weights on
  the Meituan Hugging Face org); vendor-adjacent reporting puts it at ~1.6T total, ~48B active per
  token, 1M context. The nearest open-weight checkpoint remains **LongCat-2.0** (MIT licence, with
  FP8/INT8 quantisations), and the Sep 2026 **LongCat-DeepResearch** release is explicitly
  "LongCat-2.0-based".

